## Immutable evidence identity rule

An evidence ID and a scope ID are append-only historical records. Their command, result, timestamp, environment and input binding MUST NOT be changed to describe later bytes. A later worktree requires a new scope ID and new evidence IDs. The mutable path `docs/onyx/VERIFICATION_INPUT_MANIFEST.sha256` contains only the latest canonical manifest; overwriting that path does not alter an older scope. When an older per-file manifest was not archived under an immutable path, the older record is explicitly labelled historical/unbound and cannot be reused as current proof even when its final digest is known.

