The manifest enumerates the current present files returned by `git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard`, restricted to `actions/`, `browser_tests/`, `config/`, `core/`, `dashboard/`, `memory/`, `packaging/`, `qml/`, `scripts/`, `tests/`, `.github/workflows/*.yml|yaml`, and top-level `main.py`, `ui.py`, `setup.py` and `requirements*.txt`. Paths use `/`, are ordinally sorted and each line is exactly `<lowercase-file-sha256><two spaces><normalized-relative-path><LF>`. The scope hash is SHA-256 over the complete UTF-8-without-BOM, LF-terminated manifest bytes.

Excluded deliberately: `docs/onyx` (prevents self-reference), all other documentation/plans/design artifacts, `.git`, `.venv`, build/release output, caches, `__pycache__`, generated bytecode, runtime databases/logs/uploads/secrets and tracked paths deleted in the worktree because they have no current bytes. Browser binaries and installed packages are environment dependencies rather than repository inputs; the freeze observation fingerprints the installed package listing but is not a lock file.

Recompute by applying the same enumeration/filter/order rules, hashing every present file's raw bytes, serializing the canonical lines and hashing the resulting manifest. A matching file count, every per-file digest and the final manifest digest prove only the newly assigned scope. Older evidence IDs are never reused for a later tree.

