- Verified contract: control-plane schema v1 migrates transactionally to exact schema v2 only when all M1a domain tables are empty. Enhanced registry calls deny missing, malformed, unknown, inactive and cross-workspace identities. Generic registry access cannot select `legacy-default`; only the identity-sealed host-bound adapter can create or resolve it. Marker construction, subclassing, copying, serialization and payload/environment substitution fail closed.
- Backfill evidence: the synthetic fixture contains exactly two missions (one safe completed mission assigned and one live mission pending review) plus two memories (both pending because workspace assignment is ambiguous). Those fixture databases are copied from fixed host-owned test paths into owner-only snapshots without invoking or writing the legacy stores. A verified run seals every immutable/auditable `backfill_runs` field together with the canonical result in a persisted digest; replay revalidates the exact payload contract, source identities/hashes, schema/status, timestamps, lease owner/epoch, read-back hash/counts and sidecar content. Tests independently mutate all 13 non-`run_id` run fields, every result/payload invariant and an FK-valid `run_id` graph, and each replay fails closed. Additional coverage includes semantic memory constraints, stable logical hashing, future/forged schemas, unsafe ACL/type/link sources, changed sources, partial/read-back failure, repeated execution, heartbeat lease renewal, expired-run fencing/recovery, two-thread stress and two-process convergence. Snapshot-root creation is cross-process coordinated; an existing root is owner/DACL validated without unconditional ACL mutation. Fixture mission/memory/config hashes are unchanged.
