- Verified migration contract: exact v2 structural/domain-ledger preflight runs before anchor creation and again after `BEGIN IMMEDIATE`. The locked snapshot must equal the committed anchor before any DDL. Six v2 domain tables are renamed and sealed as `legacy_v2_*`; canonical typed tables are populated through independent field-by-field re-derivation. Claim links/relations, receipt topology, request state history, event sequence/history/heads and projection revisions derive from verified hash chains, not timestamps. Fresh v3 follows the identical empty-v2 transformation.
- Verified integrity contract: normalized exact SQLite DDL SQL plus semantic schema form the persisted/anchored fingerprint. A binary type-tagged streaming root covers all relevant legacy, M1/M1b and canonical rows. The three bookkeeping tables remain outside that root to avoid circularity, but every table name, column name, cardinality and type-tagged value is separately reduced into a namespaced SHA-256 whose eight versioned 32-bit limbs are authenticated in the external HMAC journal's `entity_counts`. Commit and intent exist before prepare; the absent finalization is projected only inside the explicit prepare/recovery window and its later persisted row must match completely. Normal open requires the real row. Prepare reads the locked candidate; finalize reads a canonical read-only reopen. A v3 database remains unexposed until SQLite commit, anchor commit, exact bookkeeping binding and finalization agree.
- Security/activation limit: this is still an isolated migration-only validator, not a same-user privilege boundary or operational assistant ledger. Exact reopen/root verification is `O(N)` in database rows. M2b-c must redesign bounded canonical writer transactions and supply production host ownership; putting this migration validator on every runtime write is not accepted. Runtime/mission/permission/provider/UI integration, privilege separation and authenticated anchor-journal rotation remain later gates.

