- Verified corrective contract: after `os.open` succeeds, journal opening owns one cleanup path for ordinary errors and every `BaseException`. That path first clears its retained descriptor and identity, then closes the descriptor best-effort. A close failure cannot replace the primary exception. Direct fault seams cover `fstat`, descriptor-identity derivation, path-identity verification and platform permission application; every opened descriptor is proven closed and a clean retry succeeds. `KeyboardInterrupt`, `SystemExit` and a cancellation-style custom `BaseException` propagate by exact object identity. A failure raised by `os.open` before a descriptor exists performs no close.
- Evidence-governance correction: `VE-SCOPE-001`, `VE-UNIT-001`, `VE-PIP-001`, `VE-RUFF-001`, `VE-COMPILE-001`, `VE-SCOPE-M2BB-001` and `VE-M2B-B-001` are frozen historical records. They are not rebound to this tree. Current evidence uses new IDs and the scope-specific immutable manifest archive.
- Scope limit: this corrective record exercises the anchor implementation and audit suite plus syntax/static/diff/input checks. It does not substitute for the broader historical v3 commands in `VE-M2B-B-001`, does not claim a new whole-project run and does not change the existing default-off/non-integration, operational-writer, production-owner or M2b-c limits.

