- Verified repository contract: the sealed/private explicit-enable repository preserves the complete M2a public method signatures, dataclasses, fixed-time lifecycle outputs, ordering, errors, replay/conflict behavior and event counts. A populated immutable four-event v2 prefix reopens through v3, accepts a five-commit operational suffix on the same causal chain, passes two whole-ledger cold audits and preserves exact legacy API records. The small M2a request-update/event timestamp seam is retained honestly: exact legacy request data comes from the immutable migrated prefix while state and receipt parentage independently bind the exact source event, workspace, correlation, entity, parent IDs and digest.
- Verified commit/anchor contract: a normal mutation uses one writer session through baseline verification, prepare, SQLite commit, anchor finalize, finalization-row insert and committed verification. All five injected seams—before prepare, after prepare, after SQLite commit, after anchor finalize and after finalization row—recover to one entity, event, commit and finalization. Exact replay adds no commit. Concurrent identical attempts converge; distinct writers serialize consecutive commits. A forced 100 ms busy acquisition returns a bounded anchor conflict and leaves zero partial rows.
- Hot/cold boundary: after the first operational baseline, an incremental write succeeds with the migration cold validator and full streaming-root function replaced by fail-fast sentinels. Operational commits bind bounded row witnesses and predecessor roots. `verify_integrity()` is the explicit `O(N)` whole-ledger audit.
