- Exact operational universe: genesis and every cold audit cover **20 tables**, including `artifact_index`. A commit may contain multiple operational entries. Every audited physical row requires exactly one witness and every witness exactly one physical row; missing, extra, duplicated and semantically inconsistent rows fail closed.
- Historical-proof contract: a targeted historical read recomputes the observed row leaf, entry Merkle root, payload root, commit ID, state root and MMR leaf before traversing to the externally anchored latest root. A non-latest forgery that recomputes all downstream database commits and MMR material is rejected by the unchanged external root. `artifact_index` workspace, digest, canonical path and status are independently witnessed and semantically revalidated.
- Hot/cold contract: hot writes compare indexed latest intent and finalization heads and do not perform the prior all-intents anti-join. Targeted membership is logarithmic in the entry Merkle tree and commit MMR; normal journal work is bounded to the active generation. `verify_integrity()` and `verify_history()` remain explicit `O(N)` cold audits and check all commit/finalization gaps and all retained archive transitions.
- Journal and filesystem contract: prepare reserves capacity before append, recovery/finalization rotate as required, and no active generation exceeds **1 MiB or 512 frames**, including partial-transaction recovery seams. Archive and temporary inputs are opened as no-follow/reparse-safe regular files, identity-checked before and after bounded streaming, and size-limited before allocation. Immutable content-addressed archives are retained; no deletion policy is claimed.
- Durability contract: Windows replacement uses `MoveFileExW` with `MOVEFILE_REPLACE_EXISTING | MOVEFILE_WRITE_THROUGH`; directory-handle flushing is best effort where Windows permits it. POSIX uses atomic replacement plus directory fsync. This checkpoint claims crash-resistant publication under those stated OS contracts, not hardware power-loss immunity.
- Independent cryptographic oracle: hard-coded vectors reconstruct entry, odd-node Merkle, commit, state-root and MMR domains without importing the production private hashing helpers, preventing a shared helper bug from manufacturing its own expected values.
- Public/default-off boundary: integrity and storage failures remain fresh typed public errors without retained cause, context or private traceback chain; cancellation-style `BaseException` values propagate by identity. `ONYX_M2B_LEDGER_V3` remains strict/default-off, and startup, missions, permission, providers, tools, dashboard and UI still do not own or activate this repository.
- Residual limits: this is application-level integrity, not same-process, same-user, administrator/root, host or hardware isolation. Runtime privilege separation, production-owner wiring, provider/device execution, UI readiness, native release verification and day-to-day assistant readiness remain later gates. Immutable archives are retained and no archive deletion/retention policy is accepted here.

